@startuml
title IoT Data Sharing with fs-IBE and Dilithium-3 Trust Verification

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E6E6E6
skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #999999

actor "Regulatory Authority (TA)" as TA
participant "IoT Device" as Device
actor "User" as User
participant "Access Control & Trust Manager" as Trust
participant "Storage" as Storage
participant "IoT Edge Gateway(s)" as Gateway

== 1. System Setup & Key Generation (IBE) ==
TA -> TA: 1 Generate Public Parameters & Master Trapdoor
TA -> Device: 2 Publish Public Parameters (A)
TA -> User: 3 Generate & Send Initial Secret Key (sk) based on User ID

== 2. Data Production & Storage ==
Device -> Device: 4 Encrypt Raw Data via FS-IBE (using User ID & current Epoch)
Device -> Storage: 5 Upload Encrypted Data

== Federated Learning: Trust Model Update ==
loop Each federated training round
    Gateway -> Gateway: 5.1 Train local model on gateway traffic (raw data stays local)
    Gateway -> Gateway: 5.2 Quantize and encrypt local model update via FS-IBE\n(Aggregator ID & current Epoch)
    Gateway -> Gateway: 5.3 Sign update metadata and ciphertext digest via Dilithium-3
    Gateway -> TA: 5.4 Submit encrypted, signed update, epoch, and sample count
    TA -> TA: 5.5 Check gateway trust, epoch, and Dilithium-3 signature
    alt Update Invalid or Gateway Untrusted
        TA -> TA: 5.6 Reject update and penalize gateway trust
    else Update Valid
        TA -> TA: 5.7 Decrypt valid updates and aggregate using FedAvg
        TA -> Trust: 5.8 Provide updated global model for ML trust scoring
        TA -> Gateway: 5.9 Distribute updated global model to gateways
    end
end

== 3. Data Request & Verification ==
User -> User: 6 Create Query (Encrypted Keyword + Epoch)
User -> User: 7 Sign Query via Dilithium-3
User -> Trust: 8 Submit Signed Query Request
Trust -> Trust: 9 Check User Trust Score (TrustManager)
Trust -> Trust: 9.1 Extract Query Behavior Features & Calculate ML Trust Score\n(using latest federated model)
alt Trust Score < Threshold (Untrusted/Banned) or ML Early-Reject Condition
    Trust --> User: 10 Immediate Rejection (Access Denied)
else Trust Score >= Threshold
    Trust -> Trust: 11 Verify Dilithium-3 Signature
    alt Signature Valid
        Trust -> Trust: 11.1 Adjust Trust Score based on Signature and ML Result
    else Signature Invalid
        Trust -> Trust: 11.1 Decrease Trust Score (Score - 1)
        Trust --> User: 11.2 Query Rejected (Forged Signature)
    end
end

== 4. Data Access & Decryption ==
User -> Storage: 12 Fetch Data
Storage --> User: 13 Encrypted Data
User -> User: 14 Decrypt Data locally (using Epoch-specific Secret Key)

== 5. Forward Security (Epoch Transition) ==
TA -> Device: 15 Broadcast Epoch Tick (t -> t+1)
User -> User: 16 Local Key Evolution (Update minimal cover, delete old keys)

@enduml
